$\tfrac34 = (\tfrac34)^2 + 3(\tfrac14)^2$, confirming
Theorem~\ref{thm:energyid}. This also shows the pigeonhole bound is far from an
equality in general and that rigidity genuinely needs the uniform smallness
hypothesis.

\emph{Ball shells in the plane.} $d=2$, $R=1$, $N=4$: radii
$1, 0.8660, 0.7071, 0.5, 0$; annulus areas all $\pi/4$.

\emph{The square.} $d=2$, $K = [-1,1]^2$, $\vol(K)=4$, $N=4$: factors
$1, 0.8660, 0.7071, 0.5, 0$; layer areas $1,1,1,1$ --- identical factors to the
